# Normalise line endings per file kind.
#
# The plugin bundles are read by the browser through the Harness module loader,
# not by node or PowerShell, so their bytes must stay exactly as written: a
# checked-out CRLF copy is a different file from the tested one. Everything that
# runs in a shell keeps the platform default so Windows tooling stays happy.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets must never be touched.
*.ico binary
*.png binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
